// Generated by scripts/embed-roblox-import.mjs. Edit dist/roblox sources instead.
export const robloxImportFiles = {
  "ROBLOX-IMPORT.md": "# Import a Cuber asset into Roblox\n\nUse the included preparation script and native-Part importer. They read the exported data directly; there is no need to copy out the geometry or reconstruct the model manually. This workflow creates **block Parts joined by Motor6Ds**, never MeshParts, SpecialMeshes, or an FBX/OBJ mesh import.\n\n## Included files\n\n- `asset.json`, `atlas.png`, and optional `paint-layer/*.png`: the editable source asset. Keep these intact so the ZIP can still open in Cuber.\n- `roblox/prepare_cuber.py`: Python 3 preparation tool; standard library only. No network access or uploads.\n- `roblox/CuberImporter.lua`: Studio import ModuleScript.\n- `roblox/CuberAnimationPlayer.client.lua`: generic visual animation player; install once per experience.\n- `README.txt`: the source format, coordinates, joints, and texture-layer contract.\n\nThese files contain no game-specific image IDs, world positions, NPC behavior, or account credentials. They do not automatically upload, publish, or modify a game.\n\n## 1. Prepare the ZIP locally\n\nExtract the `roblox` folder, then run the preparer against the original asset ZIP:\n\n```sh\npython3 roblox/prepare_cuber.py \"Your-Asset.zip\" --out prepared-asset\n```\n\nIt writes `PreparedAsset.lua`, `ImageFiles.json`, `atlas.png`, and any nontransparent paint-frame PNGs. Its output lists the animation names. Preparation reads `asset.json` programmatically and prints a short summary; the full JSON does not need to be displayed. Original animation precision and keyframes are preserved. Empty animation rows remain available as rest-pose selections; duplicate names receive unique suffixes.\n\nThe preparer supports the Cuber v2 six-face box layout and checks its UV orientation. It uses the exported face normals, corrects image rotation for top/bottom faces, and keeps thin faces at least one pixel wide. Other mesh types and manually rotated/mirrored UV layouts need their own mapping; do not guess or silently substitute meshes.\n\n## 2. Upload the textures\n\nUpload the PNGs listed in `prepared-asset/ImageFiles.json` with Studio or an available upload integration, using the correct experience/account permissions. Record the image content IDs returned by the upload. Preserve the original image dimensions and transparency. If an image has not finished processing or cannot be used by the experience, resolve that before judging the texture mapping.\n\n`PaintFrames` keys are the **original zero-based layer-frame indices**, not a new sequential list of uploaded files. A nontransparent frame 0 must be supplied as `[0]`. A frame whose source `file` is null is transparent; it needs no upload or image entry. The base atlas is always displayed separately.\n\n## 3. Install the reusable scripts\n\nIn Studio **Edit mode**:\n\n1. Put `CuberImporter.lua` in a ModuleScript named `CuberImporter` in `ReplicatedStorage`.\n2. Put generated `PreparedAsset.lua` in a ModuleScript named `PreparedAsset` in `ReplicatedStorage`. Use a separate module name for each prepared asset if importing several.\n3. For animated assets, put `CuberAnimationPlayer.client.lua` in a LocalScript named `CuberAnimationPlayer` in `StarterPlayer > StarterPlayerScripts`. Install only one copy. Static rest-pose props do not need the player.\n\nThe importer creates animation ModuleScripts, so it must run from Studio's Command Bar or another permitted Studio editing context. It is not a normal gameplay server script. If using a Studio/MCP integration, use its available file/script tools to transfer these same files; no particular MCP tool names or local file-access capability are assumed.\n\n## 4. Create the model\n\nSelect the intended open place. Substitute the uploaded image IDs and the desired name, parent, placement, and uniform scale, then run this in Studio's Command Bar in Edit mode:\n\n```lua\nlocal importer = require(game.ReplicatedStorage.CuberImporter)\nlocal data = require(game.ReplicatedStorage.PreparedAsset)\n\nlocal model = importer.Import(data, {\n    Name = data.name,\n    Atlas = \"rbxassetid://YOUR_ATLAS_IMAGE_ID\",\n    -- Include every entry from ImageFiles.json.paintFrames, with its original index:\n    PaintFrames = {\n        -- [0] = \"rbxassetid://YOUR_FRAME_0_IMAGE_ID\",\n        -- [1] = \"rbxassetid://YOUR_FRAME_1_IMAGE_ID\",\n    },\n    Parent = workspace,\n    CFrame = CFrame.new(0, 0, 0),\n    Scale = 1,\n    CanCollide = false,\n    -- Animation = \"Walk\", -- Use a name printed by the preparer.\n})\n```\n\nOmit `PaintFrames` for assets without painted overlay frames. Omit `Animation` to choose Idle when present, otherwise the first animation name alphabetically. Set `Animation = \"\"` for the rig's unanimated rest pose. `CFrame` places the **authored asset origin**, not its bounding-box bottom; adjust placement if the author modeled above or below the origin. A new model is created on each import. Existing models are not deleted or replaced.\n\nAll geometry is already in Roblox coordinates: right-handed, +Y up, -Z forward, studs. Do not apply another axis flip. Quaternions are `[x,y,z,w]`; they are not Euler angles. The importer preserves `c0`, `c1`, joint hierarchy, and the invisible anchored RigRoot. The visible Parts remain unanchored and massless, connected to that root. Collisions are off by default.\n\nThe `mesh` field is only reference geometry/UV information. Painting uses six SurfaceGuis per Part, cropped ImageLabels, pixelated resampling, and a separate selected overlay. The painted atlas is not multiplied by `baseColor`. Surfaces use normal depth occlusion, not AlwaysOnTop. This approach can be UI-heavy for many complex assets; profile the target game before populating large scenes.\n\n## 5. Play animations and move the visual rig\n\nEnter Play mode to run the LocalScript. On the server, select or restart a clip with:\n\n```lua\nmodel:SetAttribute(\"Animation\", \"Walk\")\nmodel:SetAttribute(\"AnimationRate\", 1)\nmodel:SetAttribute(\"AnimationStarted\", workspace:GetServerTimeNow())\n```\n\nThe player interpolates joint translations/rotations and holds the selected paint-layer frame until the next keyframe. Non-looping clips hold their final pose and final paint frame. Empty rows reset the joints to rest. `AnimationRate` is nonnegative; setting 0 samples the start pose, not a pause-at-current-time control. Do not attach a competing Animator or another script that drives the same Motor6Ds.\n\nThe importer sets PrimaryPart to RigRoot. To place the authored origin at a new world CFrame from a server script:\n\n```lua\nlocal placement = CFrame.new(10, 0, 20)\nmodel:PivotTo(placement * model:GetAttribute(\"RootOffset\"))\n```\n\nSet the scale during import. If changing it later, update both animation translation scaling and the saved root offset as well. Root motion contained in a clip remains relative to this placement; locomotion clips may be authored in place.\n\nThis is a visual rig and client-side animation playback, not a Humanoid, player-controller, NPC AI, navigation system, or server-authoritative animated hitbox. Game code owns travel, physics, and any animation-event effects. Optional event metadata is preserved but **not executed**. For example, a laying clip does not itself spawn an egg. Animation IDs do not need publishing for this data-driven player; a separate conversion is needed for Roblox's uploaded Animation/Animator workflow.\n\n## 6. Verify in the intended experience\n\n- Expect one visible native Part per `asset.json.parts` entry, plus RigRoot, and one Motor6D per joint. There should be no MeshParts or SpecialMeshes.\n- Compare the imported asset with Cuber from all six sides. Check recognizable asymmetric details, especially front/back and top/bottom, for mirroring or rotation.\n- Verify the bind pose, connected pivots, and authored forward direction. X-axis hinges must still rotate about X.\n- Test every animation, the final frame of non-looping clips, and every painted/transparent overlay frame, including index 0 if used.\n- Check placement, scale, texture permissions, and client playback in Play mode. Visual animation does not imply server hitbox animation.\n\nThis toolkit is based on the supplied native-Part importer and has local preparation/export checks. Roblox rendering, asset permissions, and runtime integration must also be verified in the target Studio experience.\n\n## Roblox API references\n\n- Parts and joints: https://create.roblox.com/docs/reference/engine/classes/Part and https://create.roblox.com/docs/reference/engine/classes/Motor6D\n- Face images: https://create.roblox.com/docs/reference/engine/classes/SurfaceGui and https://create.roblox.com/docs/reference/engine/classes/ImageLabel\n- Model placement/scaling: https://create.roblox.com/docs/reference/engine/classes/Model\n\nNew exports preserve PNG alpha. When textureAlpha is set by the preparer, the native Part backing is transparent and its SurfaceGui images supply visible pixels. Existing bundles without that flag retain their original backing. Atlas sizes from 32 through 1024 pixels are supported.\n",
  "roblox/prepare_cuber.py": "#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Prepare a Cuber v2 asset ZIP for native Roblox Parts. Python 3, no dependencies.\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport math\nimport zipfile\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n# SurfaceGui image-right and image-down directions in Part-local coordinates.\nSURFACES = {\n    (-1, 0, 0): ('Left', (0, 0, 1), (0, -1, 0)),\n    (1, 0, 0): ('Right', (0, 0, -1), (0, -1, 0)),\n    (0, 1, 0): ('Top', (1, 0, 0), (0, 0, 1)),\n    (0, -1, 0): ('Bottom', (1, 0, 0), (0, 0, -1)),\n    (0, 0, -1): ('Front', (-1, 0, 0), (0, -1, 0)),\n    (0, 0, 1): ('Back', (1, 0, 0), (0, -1, 0)),\n}\n\n\ndef lua_string(value):\n    equals = '='\n    while ']' + equals + ']' in value:\n        equals += '='\n    return '[' + equals + '[' + value + ']' + equals + ']'\n\n\ndef dot(a, b):\n    return sum(x*y for x, y in zip(a, b))\n\n\ndef direction(a, b):\n    delta = [y-x for x, y in zip(a, b)]\n    length = math.sqrt(dot(delta, delta))\n    if length < 1e-9:\n        raise ValueError('Degenerate box face')\n    return [v/length for v in delta]\n\n\ndef face_data(mesh, index, width, height):\n    start = index * 4\n    positions = mesh['positions'][start:start+4]\n    normals = mesh['normals'][start:start+4]\n    uv = mesh['uvs'][start:start+4]\n    if len(positions) != 4 or len(uv) != 4 or len(normals) != 4:\n        raise ValueError('Expected six four-vertex box faces')\n    normal = tuple(round(v) for v in normals[0])\n    if normal not in SURFACES or any(sum(abs(v-n) for v, n in zip(row, normal)) > 1e-5 for row in normals):\n        raise ValueError('Expected axis-aligned local box normals')\n    face, right, down = SURFACES[normal]\n    xs = [v[0]*width for v in uv]\n    ys = [(1-v[1])*height for v in uv]\n    left, top, right_px, bottom = min(xs), min(ys), max(xs), max(ys)\n    if left < -1e-3 or top < -1e-3 or right_px > width+1e-3 or bottom > height+1e-3:\n        raise ValueError('UV outside atlas')\n    # Current Cuber box faces use TL, TR, BL, BR vertices in image space.\n    expected = [(left, top), (right_px, top), (left, bottom), (right_px, bottom)]\n    if any(abs(x-ex)+abs(y-ey) > 1e-3 for x, y, (ex, ey) in zip(xs, ys, expected)):\n        raise ValueError('Unsupported rotated/mirrored UV layout; keep the original Cuber export')\n    image_right = direction(positions[0], positions[1])\n    image_down = direction(positions[0], positions[2])\n    x, y = dot(image_right, right), dot(image_right, down)\n    rotation = round(math.degrees(math.atan2(y, x))) % 360\n    if rotation not in (0, 180) or dot(image_down, down) * x < .999:\n        raise ValueError('Unsupported face orientation')\n    # Remove the subpixel UV inset; keep at least one pixel for very thin parts.\n    x0, y0 = max(0, int(math.floor(left+1e-3))), max(0, int(math.floor(top+1e-3)))\n    x1, y1 = min(width, int(math.ceil(right_px-1e-3))), min(height, int(math.ceil(bottom-1e-3)))\n    return {'face': face, 'rect': [x0, y0, max(1, x1-x0), max(1, y1-y0)], 'rotation': rotation}\n\n\ndef prepare(source, destination):\n    with zipfile.ZipFile(source) as archive:\n        entries = archive.infolist()\n        if len(entries) > 512 or sum(f.file_size for f in entries) > 64*1024*1024:\n            raise ValueError('Asset ZIP is too large')\n        if len({f.filename for f in entries}) != len(entries):\n            raise ValueError('Duplicate filenames in ZIP')\n        asset = json.loads(archive.read('asset.json'))\n        if asset.get('format') != 'cube-studio-asset' or asset.get('version') != 2:\n            raise ValueError('Use a Cuber v2 asset ZIP; re-export older projects in Cuber')\n        coords = asset.get('coordinates', {})\n        if coords.get('up') != '+Y' or coords.get('forward') != '-Z' or coords.get('conversionApplied') is not True:\n            raise ValueError('Expected already-converted Roblox coordinates')\n        texture = asset['texture']\n        width, height = texture['width'], texture['height']\n        if width != height or width not in (32, 64, 128, 256, 512, 1024, 2048, 4096):\n            raise ValueError('Unsupported atlas dimensions')\n        parts = []\n        seen = set()\n        if not 1 <= len(asset['parts']) <= 128:\n            raise ValueError('Expected 1 to 128 Parts')\n        for original in asset['parts']:\n            if original.get('shape') != 'box' or original['id'] in seen:\n                raise ValueError('Expected uniquely identified box Parts')\n            seen.add(original['id'])\n            part = {k: original[k] for k in ['id', 'name', 'size', 'restTransform', 'baseColor']}\n            part['faces'] = [face_data(original['mesh'], i, width, height) for i in range(6)]\n            parts.append(part)\n        animations = {}\n        for animation in asset.get('animations', []):\n            name = animation['name']\n            if name in animations:\n                name = f'{name} [{animation[\"id\"]}]'\n            while name in animations:\n                name += '_'\n            frames = []\n            for frame in animation['keyframes']:\n                pose = {str(key): value['position'] + value['rotation'] for key, value in frame['jointTransforms'].items()}\n                frames.append({'t': frame['time'], 'p': pose, 'paint': frame.get('paintFrame', 0)})\n            animations[name] = {'frames': frames, 'duration': frames[-1]['t'] if frames else 0,\n                                'loop': animation.get('loop', True), 'events': animation.get('events', [])}\n        images = {'atlas': 'atlas.png', 'paintFrames': {}}\n        blobs = {'atlas.png': archive.read(texture['file'])}\n        for index, frame in enumerate((asset.get('paintLayer') or {}).get('frames', [])):\n            if frame.get('file'):\n                name = f'paint-frame-{index}.png'\n                blobs[name] = archive.read(frame['file'])\n                images['paintFrames'][str(index)] = name\n        prepared = {'version': 1, 'name': asset.get('name', Path(source).stem),\n                    'rigRoot': asset['rigRoot'], 'parts': parts, 'textureAlpha': texture.get('alphaMode') == 'blend',\n                    'joints': [{k: joint[k] for k in ['id', 'parentPartId', 'childPartId', 'c0', 'c1']} for joint in asset['joints']],\n                    'animations': animations, 'images': images}\n        text = json.dumps(prepared, separators=(',', ':'), allow_nan=False)\n        destination.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        (destination / 'PreparedAsset.lua').write_text('return game:GetService(\"HttpService\"):JSONDecode(' + lua_string(text) + ')\\n', encoding='utf-8')\n        (destination / 'ImageFiles.json').write_text(json.dumps(images, indent=2)+'\\n', encoding='utf-8')\n        for name, content in blobs.items():\n            (destination / name).write_bytes(content)\n    print(f'Prepared {prepared[\"name\"]}: {len(parts)} Parts, {len(animations)} animations. Output: {destination}')\n    print('Animations: ' + ', '.join(animations))\n    print('Upload the PNGs listed in ImageFiles.json; preparation does not upload anything.')\n    return prepared\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)\n    parser.add_argument('zip', type=Path)\n    parser.add_argument('--out', type=Path, default=Path('prepared-asset'))\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n    try:\n        prepare(args.zip, args.out)\n    except (ValueError, KeyError, zipfile.BadZipFile) as error:\n        parser.exit(1, f'Cannot prepare Cuber asset: {error}\\n')\n",
  "roblox/CuberImporter.lua": "-- ModuleScript for Studio's Command Bar. Creates native Parts and Motor6Ds.\nlocal HttpService = game:GetService(\"HttpService\")\nlocal CollectionService = game:GetService(\"CollectionService\")\nlocal Importer = {}\n\nlocal function frame(t)\n    local p, q = t.position, t.rotation\n    local x, y, z, w = q[1], q[2], q[3], q[4]\n    return CFrame.new(p[1], p[2], p[3],\n        1-2*(y*y+z*z), 2*(x*y-z*w), 2*(x*z+y*w),\n        2*(x*y+z*w), 1-2*(x*x+z*z), 2*(y*z-x*w),\n        2*(x*z-y*w), 2*(y*z+x*w), 1-2*(x*x+y*y))\nend\n\nlocal function longString(s)\n    local equals = \"=\"\n    while string.find(s, \"]\" .. equals .. \"]\", 1, true) do equals ..= \"=\" end\n    return \"[\" .. equals .. \"[\" .. s .. \"]\" .. equals .. \"]\"\nend\n\nfunction Importer.Import(data, options)\n    options = options or {}\n    assert(data.version == 1, \"Use the bundled prepare_cuber.py\")\n    local scale = options.Scale or 1\n    assert(type(scale) == \"number\" and scale > 0, \"Scale must be positive\")\n    assert(type(options.Atlas) == \"string\", \"Supply the uploaded atlas rbxassetid\")\n    for index in (data.images and data.images.paintFrames) or {} do\n        assert(type((options.PaintFrames or {})[tonumber(index)]) == \"string\",\n            \"Supply the uploaded image for paint frame \" .. index)\n    end\n    local animationName = options.Animation\n    if animationName == nil then\n        if data.animations.Idle then animationName = \"Idle\"\n        else\n            local names = {}\n            for name in data.animations do table.insert(names, name) end\n            table.sort(names)\n            animationName = names[1] or \"\"\n        end\n    end\n    assert(animationName == \"\" or data.animations[animationName], \"Unknown animation name\")\n    local first = data.animations[animationName] and data.animations[animationName].frames[1]\n    local initialPaint = first and first.paint or 0\n    local model = Instance.new(\"Model\")\n    model.Name = options.Name or data.name\n    local root = Instance.new(\"Part\")\n    root.Name = \"RigRoot\"\n    root.Size = Vector3.new(.2, .2, .2)\n    root.Anchored = true\n    root.Transparency = 1\n    root.CanCollide, root.CanQuery, root.CanTouch = false, false, false\n    root.CFrame = frame(data.rigRoot.restTransform)\n    root.Parent = model\n    local parts = {}\n    local count = 0\n    for _, part in data.parts do\n        local block = Instance.new(\"Part\")\n        block.Name = part.name\n        block.Size = Vector3.new(table.unpack(part.size))\n        block.CFrame = frame(part.restTransform)\n        block.Color = Color3.fromHex(part.baseColor)\n        block.Material = Enum.Material.SmoothPlastic\n        block.Transparency = data.textureAlpha and 1 or 0\n        block.Shape = Enum.PartType.Block\n        block.Anchored = false\n        block.Massless = true\n        block.CanTouch = false\n        block.CanQuery = true\n        block.CanCollide = options.CanCollide == true\n        block.TopSurface, block.BottomSurface = Enum.SurfaceType.Smooth, Enum.SurfaceType.Smooth\n        block:SetAttribute(\"CuberPartId\", part.id)\n        block.Parent = model\n        parts[part.id] = block\n        for _, face in part.faces do\n            local r = face.rect\n            local gui = Instance.new(\"SurfaceGui\")\n            gui.Name = \"Paint_\" .. face.face\n            gui.Face = Enum.NormalId[face.face]\n            gui.SizingMode = Enum.SurfaceGuiSizingMode.FixedSize\n            gui.CanvasSize = Vector2.new(r[3], r[4])\n            gui.LightInfluence = 1\n            gui.AlwaysOnTop = false\n            gui.ClipsDescendants = true\n            gui.Parent = block\n            local image = Instance.new(\"ImageLabel\")\n            image.Name = \"BaseAtlas\"\n            image.Size = UDim2.fromScale(1, 1)\n            image.AnchorPoint = Vector2.new(.5, .5)\n            image.Position = UDim2.fromScale(.5, .5)\n            image.Rotation = face.rotation or 0\n            image.ImageColor3 = Color3.new(1, 1, 1)\n            image.BackgroundTransparency = 1\n            image.BorderSizePixel = 0\n            image.Image = options.Atlas\n            image.ImageRectOffset = Vector2.new(r[1], r[2])\n            image.ImageRectSize = Vector2.new(r[3], r[4])\n            image.ResampleMode = Enum.ResamplerMode.Pixelated\n            image.Parent = gui\n            for index, textureId in options.PaintFrames or {} do\n                local overlay = image:Clone()\n                overlay.Name = \"PaintFrame_\" .. index\n                overlay:SetAttribute(\"PaintFrame\", index)\n                overlay.Image = textureId\n                overlay.Visible = index == initialPaint\n                overlay.ZIndex = 2\n                overlay.Parent = gui\n            end\n        end\n        count += 1\n        if count % 40 == 0 then task.wait() end\n    end\n    for _, joint in data.joints do\n        local motor = Instance.new(\"Motor6D\")\n        motor.Name = \"Joint_\" .. joint.id\n        motor:SetAttribute(\"CuberJointId\", tostring(joint.id))\n        -- A parent ID of zero is valid in Luau.\n        motor.Part0 = joint.parentPartId ~= nil and parts[joint.parentPartId] or root\n        motor.Part1 = parts[joint.childPartId]\n        motor.C0, motor.C1 = frame(joint.c0), frame(joint.c1)\n        motor.Parent = motor.Part0\n    end\n    local animations = Instance.new(\"Folder\")\n    animations.Name = \"CuberAnimationData\"\n    animations.Parent = model\n    for name, animation in data.animations or {} do\n        local module = Instance.new(\"ModuleScript\")\n        module.Name = name\n        module.Source = 'return game:GetService(\"HttpService\"):JSONDecode(' ..\n            longString(HttpService:JSONEncode(animation)) .. ')'\n        module.Parent = animations\n    end\n    model.WorldPivot = CFrame.identity\n    model:ScaleTo(scale)\n    model:SetAttribute(\"AnimationScale\", scale)\n    model:SetAttribute(\"CuberJointCount\", #data.joints)\n    model:SetAttribute(\"CuberAnimationCount\", #animations:GetChildren())\n    local paintCount = 0\n    for _ in options.PaintFrames or {} do paintCount += 1 end\n    model:SetAttribute(\"CuberPaintLabelCount\", #data.parts * 6 * paintCount)\n    model:SetAttribute(\"RootOffset\", root.CFrame)\n    local placement = options.CFrame or CFrame.identity\n    model:PivotTo(placement)\n    model.PrimaryPart = root\n    model:SetAttribute(\"Animation\", animationName)\n    model:SetAttribute(\"AnimationRate\", 1)\n    model:SetAttribute(\"AnimationStarted\", workspace:GetServerTimeNow())\n    model.Parent = options.Parent or workspace\n    CollectionService:AddTag(model, \"CuberAnimatedAsset\")\n    return model\nend\n\nreturn Importer\n",
  "roblox/CuberAnimationPlayer.client.lua": "-- Install once as a LocalScript in StarterPlayerScripts.\n-- Visual playback only: movement, collisions, gameplay events and AI belong to the game.\nlocal RunService = game:GetService(\"RunService\")\nlocal CollectionService = game:GetService(\"CollectionService\")\nlocal TAG = \"CuberAnimatedAsset\"\nlocal actors, pending = {}, {}\n\nlocal function transform(t, scale)\n    local x, y, z, w = t[4], t[5], t[6], t[7]\n    return CFrame.new(t[1]*scale, t[2]*scale, t[3]*scale,\n        1-2*(y*y+z*z), 2*(x*y-z*w), 2*(x*z+y*w),\n        2*(x*y+z*w), 1-2*(x*x+z*z), 2*(y*z-x*w),\n        2*(x*z-y*w), 2*(y*z+x*w), 1-2*(x*x+y*y))\nend\n\nlocal function interval(animation, time)\n    local frames = animation.frames\n    if #frames == 0 then return nil, nil, 0 end\n    if time <= frames[1].t then return frames[1], frames[1], 0 end\n    if time >= frames[#frames].t then return frames[#frames], frames[#frames], 0 end\n    for i = 1, #frames-1 do\n        if time < frames[i+1].t then\n            return frames[i], frames[i+1], (time-frames[i].t)/(frames[i+1].t-frames[i].t)\n        end\n    end\nend\n\nlocal function add(model)\n    if actors[model] or pending[model] then return end\n    local ticket = {}\n    pending[model] = ticket\n    local root = model:WaitForChild(\"RigRoot\", 15)\n    local folder = model:WaitForChild(\"CuberAnimationData\", 15)\n    if not root or not folder then\n        if pending[model] == ticket then pending[model] = nil end\n        return\n    end\n    local actor = {motors={}, paint={}, animations={}, frame=-1}\n    local deadline = os.clock()+15\n    local expected = model:GetAttribute(\"CuberJointCount\") or 0\n    while pending[model] == ticket do\n        local motors, count, paintCount = {}, 0, 0\n        for _, instance in model:GetDescendants() do\n            if instance:IsA(\"Motor6D\") then\n                local id = instance:GetAttribute(\"CuberJointId\")\n                if id then motors[id] = instance count += 1 end\n            elseif instance:IsA(\"ImageLabel\") and instance:GetAttribute(\"PaintFrame\") ~= nil then\n                paintCount += 1\n            end\n        end\n        if count >= expected and #folder:GetChildren() >= (model:GetAttribute(\"CuberAnimationCount\") or 0)\n            and paintCount >= (model:GetAttribute(\"CuberPaintLabelCount\") or 0) then\n            actor.motors = motors break\n        end\n        if os.clock() >= deadline then\n            pending[model] = nil\n            warn(\"Cuber: incomplete rig \" .. model.Name)\n            return\n        end\n        task.wait(.1)\n    end\n    if pending[model] ~= ticket then return end\n    for _, module in folder:GetChildren() do\n        if module:IsA(\"ModuleScript\") then\n            local ok, result = pcall(require, module)\n            if ok then actor.animations[module.Name] = result\n            else warn(\"Cuber: cannot load animation \" .. module.Name) end\n        end\n    end\n    for _, instance in model:GetDescendants() do\n        if instance:IsA(\"ImageLabel\") and instance:GetAttribute(\"PaintFrame\") ~= nil then\n            table.insert(actor.paint, instance)\n        end\n    end\n    if pending[model] ~= ticket then return end\n    pending[model] = nil\n    if not model:IsDescendantOf(workspace) or not CollectionService:HasTag(model, TAG) then return end\n    actors[model] = actor\n    model:SetAttribute(\"CuberAnimationReady\", true)\nend\n\nlocal function remove(model)\n    pending[model] = nil\n    local actor = actors[model]\n    if actor then\n        for _, motor in actor.motors do motor.Transform = CFrame.identity end\n    end\n    actors[model] = nil\n    model:SetAttribute(\"CuberAnimationReady\", false)\nend\n\nfor _, model in CollectionService:GetTagged(TAG) do task.spawn(add, model) end\nCollectionService:GetInstanceAddedSignal(TAG):Connect(function(model) task.spawn(add, model) end)\nCollectionService:GetInstanceRemovedSignal(TAG):Connect(remove)\n\n-- Transform is applied after PreSimulation; it is intentionally client-local.\nRunService.PreSimulation:Connect(function()\n    local now = workspace:GetServerTimeNow()\n    for model, actor in actors do\n        if not model:IsDescendantOf(workspace) then remove(model) continue end\n        local name = model:GetAttribute(\"Animation\") or \"\"\n        local animation = actor.animations[name]\n        local first, last, alpha\n        if animation then\n            local start = model:GetAttribute(\"AnimationStarted\") or now\n            local rate = math.max(0, model:GetAttribute(\"AnimationRate\") or 1)\n            local time = math.max(0, now-start)*rate\n            if animation.loop and animation.duration > 0 then time %= animation.duration\n            else time = math.min(time, animation.duration) end\n            first, last, alpha = interval(animation, time)\n        end\n        local scale = model:GetAttribute(\"AnimationScale\") or 1\n        for id, motor in actor.motors do\n            local one = first and first.p[id]\n            local two = last and last.p[id]\n            motor.Transform = one and transform(one, scale):Lerp(\n                two and transform(two, scale) or transform(one, scale), alpha) or CFrame.identity\n        end\n        -- Zero is a real overlay index; a null-file frame simply has no label.\n        local paint = first and first.paint or 0\n        if actor.frame ~= paint then\n            actor.frame = paint\n            for _, label in actor.paint do label.Visible = label:GetAttribute(\"PaintFrame\") == paint end\n        end\n    end\nend)\n"
};
